{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true},"description":"Use this when the user has job offers or candidates in 2 to 6 countries, each with its own gross salary (in USD or the local currency), and wants the total employer cost of each (e.g. \"candidate A in Poland at 240,000 PLN, candidate B in Portugal at 45k: what does each cost the company?\"). A monthly offer is passed with salary_period \"month\", which applies each country's statutory 13th or 14th month (e.g. \"un candidat \u00e0 3 000 par mois \u00e0 Madrid et un autre \u00e0 60 000 par an \u00e0 Dublin\"). Returns salary plus statutory employer charges, before any Employer of Record fee, the difference and ratio of each total to the smallest one, and the contribution ceilings each salary reaches. Rows come back in the order given. Do not use when the salary is the same in every country (use compare_countries). Data snapshot 2026-10-22. Cost comparison, not legal or tax advice.","execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"offers":{"description":"One offer per country, 2 to 6 countries, each with its own salary","items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"country":{"description":"ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 code (\"DE\") or country name (\"Germany\")","maxLength":60,"minLength":2,"type":"string"},"payments_per_year":{"description":"With salary_period \"month\" only: the total number of monthly salaries the contract pays in a year, statutory ones included (e.g. 14). Omit to use the statutory number of the country.","maximum":16,"minimum":12,"type":"number"},"salary":{"description":"Gross salary offered in this country, a year unless salary_period is \"month\"","exclusiveMinimum":0,"maximum":1000000000000,"type":"number"},"salary_currency":{"default":"USD","description":"Currency of `salary`: USD, or the local currency of the country","enum":["USD","local"],"type":"s